Suggestions:
1. Transportation: your father can drive you to the airport (saves time); if you take a taxi, leave 1.5 hours earlier (about a 45-minute drive);
2. Luggage: it is recommended to bring the woodworking notebook and commonly used tools (check them in as luggage on the plane); large equipment can be left at home;
3. Discussion meeting: your flight takes off at 19:30. If the meeting is in the afternoon or online, you can attend. It is recommended to confirm the time in advance and leave a 30-minute buffer to arrive at the airport.
In addition, Tianjin will be sunny on the 4th, 18-25°C, so no need for heavy clothing.

You can write a try-except block that first writes with UTF-8, catches UnicodeEncodeError, and automatically falls back to GBK. Code example:
try:
    df.to_csv('file.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')
except UnicodeEncodeError:
    df.to_csv('file.csv', encoding='gbk')
This way it works across platforms.
